{title: Beulah Land}
{artist: Edgar Stites & John Sweney}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
I've [F]reached the land of [Bb]corn and [F]wine, and all its riches [C]freely mine —
here [F]shines undimmed one [Bb]blissful [F]day, for all my [C]night has passed a[F]way.

Chorus
O [F]Beulah Land, sweet [Bb]Beulah [F]Land! As on thy highest [C]mount I stand,
I [F]look away across the [Bb]sea, where [F]mansions are pre[C]pared for me,
and [F]view the shining [Bb]glory [F]shore — my heaven, my [C]home forever[F]more.
